{"url": "https://www.sdstate.edu/programs/graduate/geospatial-science-engineering-phd-remote-sensing-specialization", "final_url": "https://www.sdstate.edu/programs/graduate/geospatial-science-engineering-phd-remote-sensing-specialization", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-28", "text": "Geospatial Science and Engineering (Ph.D.) \u2013 Remote Sensing Specialization | Academic Program | South Dakota State University\nSkip to main content\nApply\nVisit\nDirectories\nDegree Finder\nFaculty and Staff\nOffice Directory\nBuildings Directory\nEvent Calendar\nCampus Map\nSDSTATE\nSearch\nVisit\nDegree Finder\nCampus Map\nSDSTATE\nSearch\nFilter by Topic\nBlog Event News Profile Program\nClose Search Box\nMain Navigation\nAbout\nAbout Us\nUniversity Facts\nNews\nSandbox Login\nAwards and Rankings\nConsumer Information\nAccreditation\nAcademics\nColleges and Departments/Schools\nGeneral Education\nAcademic Calendar\nAcademic Catalog\nGraduate School\nHonors College\nLibrary\nAdmissions\nUndergraduate\nTransfer\nGraduate\nInternational\nOnline\nDual Credit\nPaying for College\nStudent Life\nHousing\nCampus Dining\nStudent Success\nStudent Experience\nUniversity Wellbeing\nParents and Families\nResearch\nEvents and Trainings\nFind Funding\nResearch Impact\nProposal Development\nResearch Support\nStudent Research Opportunities\nCommunity\nAttractions\nCamps and Conferences\nFamily Weekend\nSDState Experience\nSDSU Metro Center\nEvent Calendar\nSearch\nApply Today\nSDSTATE\nBreadcrumb\n...\nHome\nAcademics\nDegree Finder\nGeospatial Science and Engineering (Ph.D.) \u2013 Remote Sensing Specialization\nGeospatial Science and Engineering (Ph.D.) \u2013 Remote Sensing Specialization\nPh.D.\nBrookings Main Campus\nShare\nTwitter\nLinkedin\nFacebook\nEmail\nPrint\nApply Now\nMore Information\nEarth Observation\nThe geospatial science and engineering (GSE) Ph.D. is an interdisciplinary program that combines advanced coursework with cutting-edge research to advance the field of geospatial sciences. The focus is on transforming geospatial data into relevant information through acquisition, processing, characterization, analysis and modeling in order to understand geographic patterns, processes and relationships at scales ranging from landscapes to the globe.\nThe geospatial sciences integrate the geographic disciplines of cartography, geodesy, geographic information systems and remote sensing with elements of mathematics, statistics, the natural sciences, the social sciences and engineering. The resulting array of geospatial concepts, methods, technologies and datasets are used to address a wide range of pertinent questions about the functioning of the biosphere and its implications for sustainability of natural resources, agricultural productivity, biodiversity, environmental quality and human welfare in a rapidly changing world.\nCurrent faculty research interests include:\nQuantitative remote sensing\nLand cover and land use change\nGeography\nClimate change\nFire science\nApplications of geospatial technologies in agriculture, meteorology, natural resource management and other fields\nThe program seeks highly motivated students with strong backgrounds in the geospatial sciences or a closely related field to complement these efforts.\nVisit Department\nView Requirements\nCost and Aid\nQuick Facts\nLocations\nBrookings Main Campus\nCredits\n60 Credit Plan\n90 Credit Plan\nEst. Time to Completion\n3-5 years\nStart Term\nFall, Spring, Summer\nIs it for you?\nThis program will be a good fit if you:\nHave an undergraduate or master's degree in geography or a related field.\nHave a genuine curiosity about the world.\nEnjoy both the hard sciences and social sciences.\nLike working with technology.\nAre a problem-solver and analytical thinker.\nJob Outlook\nBack to top\nCareer Opportunities\nExplore possible career opportunities with this degree:\nProfessor/teacher\nRemote sensing specialist\nGIS specialist\nFederal employee\nReady to take the next step?\nContact Our Department\nBob Watrel\nVisit Department\n605-688-6288\nHelpful Resources\nProgram Requirements\nDomestic Applicants\nInternational Applicants\nTuition and Funding\nGraduate Assistantships\nApply Now\nGraduate Admissions\nGraduate School\nYou may also be interested in...\nGeospatial Science and Engineering (Ph.D.) \u2013 Geography Specialization\nGraduate\nGeospatial Intelligence Certificate (Graduate)\nCertificate\nElectrical Engineering (Ph.D.)\nGraduate\nGeography (M.S.) \u2013 Geographic Information Sciences Specialization\nGraduate\nPrecision Agriculture Certificate (Graduate)\nCertificate\nBiological Sciences (Ph.D.) \u2013 Natural Resource Management Specialization\nGraduate\nVisit Us\nCome Meet Your Future\nMeet the people that will help shape your future and define your college experience! Learn more about your academic interests with some of our world-class faculty.\nApply Today\nPlan Your Visit\nRequest Info\nGet Directions\nGive to SDSU\nOffice Directory\nExplore\nAbout SDState\nAcademics\nAdmissions\nStudent Life\nResearch\nCommunity\nConnect\nAlumni\nAthletics\nBookstore\nEvent Calendar\nGiving\nLibrary\nNews\nFor Students\nD2L\nJacks Club Hub\nJacks Email\nMyJacks Card\nMyState\nSelf Service\nFor Faculty and Staff\nEmployment\nFaculty and Staff Directory\nInsideState\nMy Account\n\u00a9 2026 All Rights Reserved.\nEmergency\nEAO\nLegal\nMission\nPolicies\nReport It\nSDState Facebook\nSDState X.com\nSDState Youtube\nSDState Instagram\nSDState LinkedIn\nSearch\nFilter by Topic\nBlog Event News Profile Program\nAbout\nAbout Us\nUniversity Facts\nNews\nSandbox Login\nAwards and Rankings\nConsumer Information\nAccreditation\nAcademics\nColleges and Departments/Schools\nGeneral Education\nAcademic Calendar\nAcademic Catalog\nGraduate School\nHonors College\nLibrary\nAdmissions\nUndergraduate\nTransfer\nGraduate\nInternational\nOnline\nDual Credit\nPaying for College\nStudent Life\nHousing\nCampus Dining\nStudent Success\nSt